// ---- Compute features: what a GPU offers for compute, asked for, and enabled ----
//
// The device 'requestDevice' makes enables only what drawing needs. Compute
// that moves a lot of numbers (a language model's weights, quantised to 8 or
// 4 bits a value, multiplied by 16-bit or 32-bit activations) wants more, and
// each of it is optional in Vulkan, so a GPU is asked what it has, a program
// asks for what it wants, and the device is made with the ones both name:
//
//   imm has = adapter.computeCapabilities();         // a plain value: what this GPU offers
//   if has.float16Arithmetic and has.integerDotProduct { ... }
//   mut device = adapter.requestComputeDevice(&ComputeRequest.all());   // or ask for some
//   device.compute.float16Arithmetic                 // what the device was made with
//
// What is queried (Vulkan 1.1 to 1.3's core features and limits, through
// vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 and vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2; nothing is
// an extension):
//   - 16-bit floats: shaderFloat16 (arithmetic), storageBuffer16BitAccess and
//     uniformAndStorageBuffer16BitAccess (storage); 16-bit integers: shaderInt16;
//   - 8-bit integers: shaderInt8 (arithmetic), storageBuffer8BitAccess and
//     uniformAndStorageBuffer8BitAccess (storage);
//   - integer dot product: shaderIntegerDotProduct, and which forms the GPU
//     does in hardware ('dot4x8Packed...Accelerated': four signed or unsigned
//     bytes packed in a u32, multiplied and added: Slang's dot4add_i8packed and
//     dot4add_u8packed, SPIR-V's OpSDot and OpUDot);
//   - shaderSubgroupExtendedTypes: subgroup operations on 16-bit and 8-bit values;
//   - the subgroup (a GPU's warp or wave): its size, the range of sizes, the
//     shader stages that have subgroup operations (this layer's SHADER_STAGE_...
//     bits) and which operations (SUBGROUP_OP_... bits, Vulkan's);
//   - limits: maxBufferSize, maxMemoryAllocationSize, maxStorageBufferRange,
//     maxPerStageDescriptorStorageBuffers, the compute workgroup and its
//     shared memory, the storage buffer offset alignment, and the sizes of
//     the memory heaps ('Adapter.memoryHeaps').
//
// What is enabled, and when. 'requestDevice' and 'requestDeviceWith' enable
// none of it, exactly as before (a drawing program's device is unchanged), and
// 'device.compute' says so (its flags false, its numbers still the GPU's).
// 'requestComputeDevice' enables a feature when it is asked for in the
// 'ComputeRequest' AND the GPU has it; one asked for and absent is not an
// error, 'device.compute' tells. A shader whose SPIR-V declares a capability
// that needs a feature the device did not enable ('createShaderModule') is
